  "asr_text": "But when I take the writer's side, things suddenly get complicated. I might ask AI to fix a phrase or talk through the plot, but how far can I go and still proudly say, I wrote this? Where is the line between a helpful partner to talk things over with and a co-writer? So it would be a shame to reduce this prize to a simple choice: is AI good or bad? A prize that is supposed to choose works also shines a light on the values of the people doing the choosing. It makes the question of whether AI was used not the end of the discussion, but the starting point for reading. It seems that writers are not the only ones being tested at this new entrance. So, how will we read that book?",
